```java
public class LongestPalindromicSubsequence {

    // Function to find the length of the longest palindromic subsequence
    public static int longestPalindromicSubsequence(String text) {
        int n = text.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[n][n];

        // All single character substrings are palindromes of length 1
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            dp[i][i] = 1;
        }

        // Build the dp table in bottom-up manner
        for (int length = 2; length <= n; length++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < n - length + 1; i++) {
                int j = i + length - 1;
                if (text.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j) && length == 2) {
                    dp[i][j] = 2;
                } else if (text.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j)) {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2;
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j]);
                }
            }
        }

        return dp[0][n - 1];
    }

    // Function to retrieve the longest palindromic subsequence
    public static String findLongestPalindromicSubsequence(String text) {
        int n = text.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[n][n];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            dp[i][i] = 1;
        }

        for (int length = 2; length <= n; length++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < n - length + 1; i++) {
                int j = i + length - 1;
                if (text.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j) && length == 2) {
                    dp[i][j] = 2;
                } else if (text.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j)) {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2;
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i][j - 1], dp[i + 1][j]);
                }
            }
        }

        // Reconstruct the longest palindromic subsequence
        StringBuilder lps = new StringBuilder();
        int i = 0, j = n - 1;
        while (i <= j) {
            if (text.charAt(i) == text.charAt(j)) {
                lps.insert(lps.length()/2, text.charAt(i));
                i++;
                j--;
            } else if (dp[i][j - 1] > dp[i + 1][j]) {
                j--;
            } else {
                i++;
            }
        }

        // Return the final lps.
        return lps.toString();
    }

    // Main function to test the utility
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String text = "babad";
        System.out.println("Input text sequence: " + text);
        String longestPalindromicSubsequence = findLongestPalindromicSubsequence(text);
        System.out.println("Longest Palindromic Subsequence: " + longestPalindromicSubsequence);
        System.out.println("Length of Longest Palindromic Subsequence: " + longestPalindromicSubsequence.length());
    }
}
```

This program performs the following tasks:
1. Uses dynamic programming (`dp` array) to compute the length of the longest palindromic subsequence.
2. Constructs the longest palindromic subsequence from the `dp` array.
3. Outputs the longest palindromic subsequence and its length when run with the input text "babad".

When you run this program with the input "babad", it will correctly find and print the longest palindromic subsequence.

