```php
<?php
function getStringLength($str) {
    $length = 0;

    // Traverse through the string until we hit the null byte (end of string)
    while (isset($str[$length])) {
        $length++;
    }

    return $length;
}

// Example usage
$myString = "Hello, world!";
echo "The length of the string is: " . getStringLength($myString);
?>
```

This code defines a function `getStringLength` that manually counts the characters in the input string. It starts from the beginning of the string and increments a counter until it reaches a character position that is not set (which indicates the end of the string). This approach avoids using any built-in string length functions.
